WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.403
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.474
JOE BIDEN:<i> We're ending
 America's longest war.</i>

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.642
SPEAKER:<i> Twenty years.</i>

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.512
It's obviously not a success.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.851
We knew we were there
to evacuate the at-risk Afghans.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.352
<i> You know, the US citizens.</i>

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:23.189
SPEAKER 2:<i> They kinda
 made it sound like, "Oh,
it's gonna be quick and simple.</i>

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.757
<i> We're gonna be in and out."</i>

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:25.825
(DISTANT EXPLOSION)

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.761
But that didn't happen here.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.696
SOLDIER: You need to back up.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.365
(CROWD CLAMORING)

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.134
Push back!

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.304
SPEAKER 3:<i> It was very
 dark times in Afghanistan,</i>

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:39.939
<i> when Taliban take over.</i>

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.809
SPEAKER 4:<i> I was told
 that if you do not leave</i>

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.444
<i> in the coming three days,</i>

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.445
you will be assassinated.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.449
We've got thousands of people,
panicked.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.417
SPEAKER 5:
<i> The runway was the mission.</i>

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.119
Keep the runway open
at all costs.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.755 line:0%
(SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.760
The government had collapsed.
The Afghan president was gone.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.130
I'm being told, "Hey, we're
working with the Taliban now."

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.504 line:0%
(SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:16.176
Our mission was to not let
anyone to leave the country.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.112
SPEAKER 6:<i> The situation
 on the ground</i>

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.914
<i> is something like I've never
 experienced before.</i>

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:23.583
<i> In any of my deployments.</i>

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.119
Everyone was moving
toward the airport.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:30.423 line:0%
(SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.592
You never want to tell your men
you don't know what to do.

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.060
(SCATTERED YELLING)

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.195
Push back!

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:37.597
SPEAKER 7:
<i> I had no idea what to do.</i>

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.101
SPEAKER 2:<i> Please, let us,
 like, just get out of here.</i>

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:42.568
(SCREAMING)

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.738
You leave a place where
you never think you'll leave.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.507
(PEOPLE YELLING)

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.845
But you leave it
because you can't live.

